{
  "dom_id": "step-q5288",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Find the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence if the first term is $5$ and the common difference is $1.$",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the first term is ${a}_{1}=5$ and the common difference is $d=1.$ So, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =5+(n-1)(1) \\\\  & =5+n-1 \\\\  & =4+n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the formula for the $n$th term is ${a}_{n}=4+n.$",
